id: ops-cl0o
title: "Adding a source file breaks the coverage gate in three places, and none of them says so"
description: "The coverage gate enumerates every source file so that a file added without tests cannot pass by being absent from the report. That enumeration is duplicated by hand in three fixture lists inside test/coverage-gate.test.ts (a POSIX stub, a Windows stub, and an explicit array) plus the include list in the package coverage script. Adding one source file therefore requires four coordinated edits, and omitting any of them fails the gate with a coverage threshold error that names a percentage rather than the missing file. Two source files added in this session each hit it."
type: Issue
status: blocked
priority: 2
tags[3]: "area:release","area:testing","type:defect"
created_at: "2026-08-28T14:25:04.891Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-02T23:58:00.687Z"
author: claude
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "New TypeScript modules require no edits to hard-coded coverage fixture lists; overlapping source roots produce a sorted unique required-file denominator; real c8 accepts a newly tested module and rejects an unimported module by filename at unchanged per-file 100/100/100/100 thresholds; CLI/SDK 2026.9.29 and the lockfile pass package release checks; required exact-head reviews complete before merge; Each c8 invocation owns unique reports and raw counters, preserves an enclosing default coverage/tmp, rejects stale reports, and passes two real concurrent processes in the same repository; Starting or failing a coverage gate invalidates the shared LCOV so the real assurance provider refuses earlier passing measurements after a test-only failure"
definition_of_ready: Canonical pm-ops checkout and tracker verified; no other claim or active checkout process; stacked on the existing TSX gate candidate
risk: low
blocked_by: ops-0c8k
blocked_reason: "Full documentation under ops-0c8k remains incomplete at 590/1887 declarations and 22/23 modules. Parent PR132 and complete exact-head reviews remain required. Bun strict health fails in the released core under upstream1349. Default CI skips two opt-in fleet checks, and local Trivy/ShellCheck are unavailable. No publication or deployment."
repro_steps: Configure overlapping coverageGate.sources entries and run node --test test/coverage-gate.test.ts. A nested c8 invocation previously inherited and cleaned the enclosing raw-counter directory.
expected_result: "New source modules are discovered once in deterministic order without fixture list edits, while nested coverage invocations preserve parent data and all required measured gates remain enforced."
actual_result: Sorted unique source scope is independently verified; isolated c8 reports and counters preserve parent/peer data; shared LCOV invalidates on pending or failing runs so actual assurance consumers refuse earlier passing reports
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  ops-0c8k,blocked_by,"2026-09-29T20:12:55.918Z",codex-coverage-inventory,"cli:update:blocked_by",detected
comments[8]:
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T18:30:48.281Z"
    author: pi-glm
    text: "Land-pass update (pi-glm, orchestrator): PR #134's last open reviewer finding (CodeRabbit 4138483396, readdirSync order nondeterminism in the coverage-gate test assertions) is valid and fixed in b5463c8 - all three directory listings are sorted before deepStrictEqual. Thread resolved. Head rebased onto the pm-ops#132 head f3e66c3 (current main 2026.9.29) and re-verified: focused 11-test coverage suite passes; full npm run release:check passes 456 tests, 0 failures, 2 existing opt-in real-data skips, coverage-gate 23 sources at 100/100/100/100. All bot review bodies and comments now carry reactions; re-review requested from CodeRabbit/Greptile/Gemini on the new head."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T18:35:24.315Z"
    author: pi-glm
    text: "Evidence clarification: the pm test --run wrapper was interrupted by its own execution timeout mid-suite (node --test reports ops.test.ts interrupted at ~89s into that file, trust_refusal on one sub-command), not by a gate failure. Direct verification on the same head: full 'npm run release:check' completed with exit 0 (456 tests, 0 failures, 2 existing opt-in real-data skips; coverage-gate 23 sources at 100/100/100/100), and the focused 'node --test test/coverage-gate.test.ts' passed 11/11."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T21:02:27.848Z"
    author: pi-grok
    text: "Cubic review 5395445424 disposition:\n\n4168720012 is valid as an evidence clarification, not a history rewrite. Appended a note that separates the opted-in PM_OPS_TEST_REPOS run (zero skips) from the default suite (exactly two real-data skips in test/ops.test.ts). Hashed note_add lines were kept.\n\n4168720026 is valid. renameSync was the only post-validation failure that escaped failRun, so a locked canonical lcov bypassed the injected exit boundary. A red test failed first with Missing expected exception. The publisher is now caught and routed through failRun(1); production still uses renameSync."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T21:03:51.083Z"
    author: pi-grok
    text: "Focused red-green evidence: node --test --test-name-pattern 'failed canonical report publish' test/coverage-gate.test.ts failed first with Missing expected exception, then passed after the publisher catch. Full node --test test/coverage-gate.test.ts then passed 12/12."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T21:09:41.775Z"
    author: pi-grok
    text: "Land-pass gate on the rebased stack: npm run release:check exited 0. node --test reported 457 tests, 455 pass, 0 fail, 2 skipped (the default-suite real-data tests). The total is 457 rather than the earlier 456 because this branch adds the failed-publish-path coverage-gate test; the 2 skips are unchanged. coverage-gate reported 23 sources at 100/100/100/100. changelog:check, audit:prod, pack:dry-run, and the release verifiers passed. pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers exited 0."
    edited_at: "2026-10-02T21:16:42.259Z"
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T23:46:03.289Z"
    author: codex-sol-land
    text: "Resumed PR #134 from 930f66437a4a7f664891d68a5783b49ed26d41f3. Rebase onto current fix/pm-ops-tsx-quality-gates-2026-09-28 yields cf970b002185c956200fb0a8a9195f85c3bd25b1. All existing bot artifacts and restart-era owner replies inspected; no new actionable finding. Preserve earlier fixes and technical refusals. Verifying unchanged CI gates under the shared heavy lock; no merge, release or closure."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T23:48:05.924Z"
    author: codex-sol-land
    text: "Restart focused selection exposed an existing linked-test context incompatibility: none/source is refused by current CLI because source workspace can discover tracker data. Its source/schema counterpart passes 12/12. Preserve that counterpart; replace only the incompatible context entry with the same command in none/snapshot, retaining all history and trust policy. This tightens isolation, changes no gate/test assertion, and enables the intended synthetic acceptance. Full CI gate still needs its own passing run."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T23:57:59.601Z"
    author: codex-sol-land
    text: "Resumed verification: npm ci, current-base rebase, fresh committed-dist comparison, strict local tracker health with required merge drivers, npm run release:check, and bun install --no-save all passed. Full gate: 457 tests, 455 pass, 2 skips; configured coverage thresholds unchanged. PM-linked test/coverage-gate.test.ts passed. Earlier findings and technical refusals retained; no new source fix was needed in this restart. Exact pushed-head CI and substantive reviewer availability remain separate checks; no merge, release, publication or item closure."
notes[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T19:54:12.169Z",codex-coverage-inventory,"Scope: consolidate fixture source reports around the gates emitted include arguments while retaining independent real-c8 pass/fail fixtures. Deduplicate and sort overlapping source roots. Update exact published CLI/SDK pin to 2026.9.29. Depends on parent TSX-gate candidate PR132. Rollout: reviewed source PR only, no publication/deployment. Rollback: revert this change; thresholds/exemptions remain unchanged."
  "2026-09-29T20:01:49.136Z",codex-coverage-inventory,"Red-green evidence: duplicate-root regression failed with four include entries instead of two. Real child c8 initially inherited Node test-worker context and skipped execution; standalone child environment now executes its real assertions. Full release gate then exposed c8 inheriting and cleaning parent NODE_V8_COVERAGE counters, yielding incomplete aggregate coverage. Added a red runner-argument regression and pinned each gate to its repository-owned coverage/tmp. Exact development-version assertion updated alongside the published CLI pin; thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-09-29T20:12:55.278Z",codex-coverage-inventory,"Validated source candidate: npm ci and exact CLI/SDK 2026.9.29 pin pass. Full release:check with real pm-slack and pm-csv selections passes 456/456 tests, zero skips/TODOs, c8 per-file 100 statements/branches/functions/lines across 23 runtime/tooling/template files, 221 selected documented declarations, zero duplication across 43 sources and zero full/production dependency audit findings. PM-linked none/snapshot acceptance passes 11 tests. The default suite still skips two opt-in live-fleet checks. Independent full documentation presence census is 580/1879 declarations and 22/23 module docblocks, tracked by ops-0c8k. Selected docstring gate success is not full documentation coverage. No publication or deployment is authorized by these measurements."
  "2026-09-29T20:22:05.110Z",codex-coverage-inventory,"Review round at dbb0265: Sourcery inline 4137899586 correctly identified collisions for concurrent or nested invocations within one repository. Upvoted and replied with the disposition. Reclaimed this owner for the fix: per-invocation report/counter directories, successful atomic LCOV publication, cleanup and real concurrent process acceptance. Full documentation and broader gate blockers remain."
  "2026-09-29T20:36:19.460Z",codex-coverage-inventory,"CI round at dbb0265 ran its coverage jobs successfully but failed changelog:check: a fresh checkout sees the already published v2026.09.29 tag while the local clone had stale tags. Fetching writable pm-ops refs reproduced the failure locally. Regenerated CHANGELOG.md with pm-changelog, changing only the existing Unreleased heading to 2026.9.29 - 2026-09-29. No release or publication is being created. Independent inventory omission proof fails on index.ts. New broader documentation census: 582/1883 declarations and 22/23 module docblocks, still incomplete."
  "2026-09-29T20:38:33.655Z",codex-coverage-inventory,"Review fixes validated: each gate owns coverage/run-* reports and raw counters, publishes the last successful LCOV atomically, and removes its own temporary artifacts on success or handled failure. Real c8 passes two concurrent same-repository processes and preserves the default parent coverage/tmp sentinel across successful and failing runs. Independent fast-glob inventory covers the actual package; deliberately omitting index.ts fails its assertion. Full release:check passes 456 tests with zero failures/skips/TODOs and all four c8 columns at 100 per-file across 23 files. PM-linked none/snapshot acceptance passes 11 tests. Full/production audits have zero findings, strict health/validate/history pass. Generated changelog is current after writable tag refresh. All four valid inline findings have been upvoted and acknowledged; exact-head review of the fix remains pending."
  "2026-09-29T21:00:57.706Z",codex-coverage-inventory,"Greptile round 2 finding 4138181201 at f801740 is valid: retaining earlier canonical LCOV after a failed run lets the real assurance provider report an old pass after only tests change. Reclaimed for a fail-closed report fix. New real-provider regression resolves 100 from a successful c8 report, changes only a test, observes gate exit 1, then requires the provider to refuse the absent report. It fails against f801740 with Missing expected exception. Focused and PM-linked acceptance now pass 11 tests without skips. Every start and every exit, including preflight, invalidates the canonical report; unexpected failures invalidate through finally. Successful peers retain isolated counters and publish atomically. Full gate validation is running."
  "2026-09-29T21:10:45.798Z",codex-coverage-inventory,"Final assurance source passes full release:check: 456 tests, zero failures/skips/TODOs, all four c8 columns at 100 per-file over 23 runtime/tooling/template files. PM-linked none/snapshot acceptance passes 11 tests. The real provider reads 100 from a successful report, then refuses it after only the tests change and fail. Pre-fix f801740 fails this assertion. Broader documentation presence is now 590/1887 declarations and 22/23 modules after documenting every newly introduced internal boundary/path/state declaration. Selected docstrings still checks 221 declarations, not the complete scope. npm packed strict health passes; Bun imports, extension copy/execution and all five adapter configurations pass but strict health reproduces upstream1349 without extensions. No duplicate upstream write or workaround. Exact-head new checks and reviews remain necessary after this final fix."
  "2026-10-02T21:01:15.869Z",pi-grok,"Clarification for cubic 4168720012: the 2026-09-29T20:12:55 note describes two different invocations, which is why it says both zero skips and two skips. test/ops.test.ts skips \"real-data: scan on configured pm repos reports all ready\" and \"real-data: verify-release on second configured pm repo passes\" unless PM_OPS_TEST_REPOS names at least two existing package roots. A release:check that sets that variable to real pm-slack and pm-csv roots can report 456 tests and zero skips. The default invocation, including CI and the 2026-10-02 land-pass rerun, leaves PM_OPS_TEST_REPOS unset and therefore skips exactly those two tests: 456 tests, 0 failures, 2 skips. Later notes that say zero skips without that qualifier mean the opted-in selection, not the default suite. Hashed history lines are unchanged; this note is the accurate default-suite count."
